# /etc/wg-failover/wg0.peers  — rename to drop .example to activate
#
#   public_key|endpoint_host|endpoint_port|description
#
# Each Proton server has its own public key, so a candidate is a (key,
# endpoint) pair — you cannot keep the key and swap only the host. Generate
# several configs against the same private key and lift the pairs out.
#
# Port 443 throughout: Digi/RCS-RDS filters UDP 51820.
#
# Order does not matter; the script re-ranks by RTT hourly and caches to
# /var/run/wg-failover/wg0.ranked. Force a re-rank with:
#   rm /var/run/wg-failover/*.ranked.at
#
# aBcD...=|193.148.16.10|443|CH-AT#1 secure core
# eFgH...=|193.148.16.11|443|CH-AT#2 secure core
# iJkL...=|185.159.157.20|443|CH#5
